{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Elab/Tactic/Grind/Param.html#Lean.Elab.Tactic.Grind.withParams\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Elab</span>.<span class=\"name\">Tactic</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">withParams</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">params</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Main.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Params\">Meta.Grind.Params</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">ps</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.TSyntaxArray\">TSyntaxArray</a> <span class=\"fn\">`Lean.Parser.Tactic.grindParam</span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">only</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">k</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Elab/Tactic/Grind/Basic.html#Lean.Elab.Tactic.Grind.GrindTacticM\">GrindTacticM</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Elab/Tactic/Grind/Basic.html#Lean.Elab.Tactic.Grind.GrindTacticM\">GrindTacticM</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Helper method for processing parameters in tactics such as `finish` and `finish?`","docLink":"./Lean/Elab/Tactic/Grind/Param.html#Lean.Elab.Tactic.Grind.withParams","kind":"def","line":431,"name":"Lean.Elab.Tactic.Grind.withParams","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Elab/Tactic/Grind/Param.lean#L431-L462"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Elab/Tactic/Grind/Param.html#Lean.Elab.Tactic.Grind.getPreservedParams\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Elab</span>.<span class=\"name\">Tactic</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">getPreservedParams</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">params</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Array\">Array</a> (<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.TSyntax\">TSyntax</a> <span class=\"fn\">`Lean.Parser.Tactic.grindParam</span>)</span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Elab/Term/TermElabM.html#Lean.Elab.Term.TermElabM\">TermElabM</a> <span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Array\">Array</a> (<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.TSyntax\">TSyntax</a> <span class=\"fn\">`Lean.Parser.Tactic.grindParam</span>))</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Returns the parameters of a `grind?`/`finish?` call that the suggested tactic must carry\nverbatim.\n\nParameters that produce E-matching theorems are recorded in the generated script as\n`use`/`instantiate` steps and are omitted. The remaining parameters have effects the script\ncannot represent, so dropping them produces suggestions that fail during replay:\n- modifiers that do not create E-matching theorems (`cases`, `inj`, `funCC`, `symbol`);\n- identifiers resolving to a type marked for case-splitting (e.g., `[EqvGen]` for an\n  inductive predicate);\n- identifiers resolving to a theorem whose statement is not a `∀` and is not indexable (see\n  `isFactDecl`), which is asserted as a fact rather than recorded as an E-matching theorem;\n- identifiers using local variable dot notation (e.g., `cs.getD_rightInvSeq` where `cs` is a\n  local variable), which produce anchors that need the original term during replay;\n- non-identifier terms (e.g., `show p by tac`).\n\n**TODO**: This syntactic filtering is a stopgap: it duplicates parameter-elaboration logic\nand silently depends on which side effects are representable in scripts. A more robust\nsolution is to make the script self-contained, e.g., a script step that marks a type for\ncase-splitting, and tracking which parameters were actually used.","docLink":"./Lean/Elab/Tactic/Grind/Param.html#Lean.Elab.Tactic.Grind.getPreservedParams","kind":"def","line":387,"name":"Lean.Elab.Tactic.Grind.getPreservedParams","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Elab/Tactic/Grind/Param.lean#L387-L429"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Elab/Tactic/Grind/Param.html#Lean.Elab.Tactic.elabGrindParams\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Elab</span>.<span class=\"name\">Tactic</span>.<span class=\"name\">elabGrindParams</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">params</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Main.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Params\">Meta.Grind.Params</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">ps</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.TSyntaxArray\">TSyntaxArray</a> <span class=\"fn\">`Lean.Parser.Tactic.grindParam</span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">only</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">lax </span><span class=\"fn\">incremental</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a> := <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.false\">false</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Elab/Term/TermElabM.html#Lean.Elab.Term.TermElabM\">TermElabM</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Main.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Params\">Meta.Grind.Params</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Elaborates `grind` parameters.\n`incremental = true` for tactics such as `finish`, in this case, we disable some kinds of parameters\nsuch as `- ident`.","docLink":"./Lean/Elab/Tactic/Grind/Param.html#Lean.Elab.Tactic.elabGrindParams","kind":"def","line":314,"name":"Lean.Elab.Tactic.elabGrindParams","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Elab/Tactic/Grind/Param.lean#L314-L360"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Elab/Tactic/Grind/Param.html#Lean.Elab.Tactic.addEMatchTheorem\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Elab</span>.<span class=\"name\">Tactic</span>.<span class=\"name\">addEMatchTheorem</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">params</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Main.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Params\">Meta.Grind.Params</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">id</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Meta/Defs.html#Lean.Syntax.Ident\">Ident</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">declName</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Name\">Name</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">kind</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Extension.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.EMatchTheoremKind\">Meta.Grind.EMatchTheoremKind</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">minIndexable</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">suggest</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a> := <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.false\">false</a>)</span></span> <span class